  "date": "2020-08",
  "title": "Coffee Lectures In 10 Minuten Zu Neuem Knowhow",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "How the Coffee Lectures work",
      "text": "- Nexis Uni: Find useful press articles from all over the world easily, 2 September\n\n- What the hell is a postprint? Green open-access publishing in a nutshell, 9 September\n\n- Data management plan (DMP) for the SNSF: What does it mean for me? 16 September\n\n- Comparing the bibliographic management systems Mendeley and EndNote, 23 September\n\n- Fantastic library services and where to find them – Quick guide for new staff and doctoral students, 30 September\n\nIn our Coffee Lectures , you can find out about new tools to assist you in your academic work and learn important tips and tricks on topics including open access and the creation of a data management plan for your project application with the Swiss National Science Foundation (SNSF)."
    },
    {
      "heading": "How the Coffee Lectures work",
      "text": "Each session lasts ten minutes. You will receive concise, condensed information on a particular topic and have time to ask questions at the end. Just the right length of time to enjoy a coffee while you listen."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Subscribe to Newsletter",
      "text": "The online events will be held via Zoom at 3.15 p.m. on Wednesday afternoons in September 2020. Registration is not required.\n\nThe sessions are held in English, with the exception of the first Coffee Lecture (German).\n\nFor browser-based Zoom sessions, we recommend using Chrome."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Topics in September 2020",
      "text": "#KnowHow – The ETH Library’s infrastructure and tools lead you to your goal.\n\n#ETHLibraryDigital – The ETH Library is there for you digitally with various resources and services , not only during the COVID-19 protective measures."
    }
  ],
